    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d739">

                <pb facs="1090" n="990" xml:id="pg990"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.42157 Detroit/79</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Canada</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Robbins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 544</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-04-21">April 21,
                        1934</date>.<lb/>[Received April 30.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s instruction No. 257 of March 13, 1934, (file No. 711.42157
                    Detroit/67) and to my despatch No. 543 of today’s date, and to enclose herewith
                    copy of a note received this morning from the Secretary of State for External
                    Affairs setting forth certain observations with regard to the dredging
                    operations being carried out by the United States Government in the St. Clair
                    River.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren D. Robbins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d739-a1.xml" xpointer="d739-a1"/>
            </div>
